==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Removing the closed-world Allowed assignment lets Alloy add arbitrary (Relationship, OperationKind) pairs; injecting ComplianceOfficerRel -> GetRecord forces a state where a compliance officer can read clinical content, directly violating LeastPrivilege and FR_007.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_007_ComplianceContentBlind, FR_004_CareTeamGating, FR_018_AccessLogComplianceOnly
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_007_ComplianceContentBlind: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_CareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AccessLogComplianceOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditBijection  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_AuditBijection.als
    rationale: Removing F_AuditBijection breaks the surjectivity and injectivity of opAudit; injecting an orphan AuditEntry (with no owning Operation) forces a state where an audit entry exists without a matching access attempt — violating the always-on audit bijection.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_013_AlwaysOnAudit, FR_017_AuditRetention
      - AuditCompleteness: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_013_AlwaysOnAudit: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_017_AuditRetention: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttributionCorrect  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_AuditAttributionCorrect.als
    rationale: Removing F_AuditAttributionCorrect breaks the requirement that entryRole matches the caller's role; injecting a mismatch forces a state where an operation's audit entry records the wrong role, violating attribution correctness.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_014_AuditEntryFields, FR_015_AuditImmutable
      - AttributionCorrectness: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_014_AuditEntryFields: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_015_AuditImmutable: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_NotesOnlyFromPermittedAppend  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_NotesOnlyFromPermittedAppend.als
    rationale: Removing F_NotesOnlyFromPermittedAppend lets ClinicalNote atoms exist without a backing permitted PostNote operation; injecting an orphan note forces the model to contain a note that was never created by an authorised append, directly violating the append-only invariant.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_012_NotesAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_012_NotesAppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_PatientAssignedRecordPairing  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_PatientAssignedRecordPairing.als
    rationale: Removing F_PatientAssignedRecordPairing allows a Patient to have no assignedRecord or an extra assignedRecord; injecting a patient without an assignedRecord causes the PatientOwn relationship to become impossible to satisfy, undermining ownership-based access control.
    expected to FAIL: FR_003_PatientAssignedRecord, FR_006_PatientSelfAccess, OwnershipBasedAccess
      - FR_003_PatientAssignedRecord: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_PatientSelfAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OutcomeFromPermissionMatrix  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_OutcomeFromPermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Removing F_OutcomeFromPermissionMatrix severs the tie between the Allowed matrix and opOutcome; injecting a NonCareTeamClinician operation with Permitted outcome on GetRecord forces the model into a state that violates the care-team gating and least-privilege invariants simultaneously.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_004_CareTeamGating, FR_006_PatientSelfAccess, FR_007_ComplianceContentBlind, NoInformationLeakage
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_CareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_PatientSelfAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_007_ComplianceContentBlind: FAIL (expected)
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)

